# Loaded automatically by `next build` (NODE_ENV=production), so the Vercel
# deployment points at the live Railway backend with no dashboard configuration.
#
# This is committed on purpose. Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the
# client bundle at build time, so it is public by construction — it is a hostname,
# not a credential. Committing it removes a silent failure mode: without it, a
# missing dashboard variable falls back to http://localhost:8000 (see lib/api.ts),
# and the deployed site would try to call the visitor's own machine.
#
# A variable set in the Vercel dashboard still wins — Next.js never overrides a
# value already present in the environment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://typeform-production-bd2b.up.railway.app
